## 5. Advanced Argo CD Structures: AppProject & ApplicationSet

To prevent configuration sprawl and ensure multi-tenant security, enterprises rely on `AppProject` and `ApplicationSet` CRDs.

### Argo CD AppProject (The Security Firewall)
An `AppProject` provides a logical sandbox. It ensures that a specific development team can only deploy certain applications to designated clusters and namespaces.

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: AppProject
metadata:
  name: payment-team-project
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  description: "Security boundary for the Payments team engineering workloads"
  destinations:
    - name: spoke-staging
      namespace: payments
    - name: spoke-production
      namespace: payments
  sourceRepos:
    - 'https://github.com'
  clusterResourceWhitelist:
    - group: ''
      kind: Namespace
  namespaceResourceWhitelist:
    - group: '*'
      kind: '*'
```

### Argo CD ApplicationSet (The Automation Engine)
Instead of manually creating individual Argo CD application manifests for every environment, an `ApplicationSet` uses **Generators** to automatically discover target configurations and deploy them uniformly.

```yaml
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: ApplicationSet
metadata:
  name: payment-service-appset
  namespace: argocd
spec:
  generators:
    - list:
        elements:
          - cluster: spoke-staging
            url: https://10.100.0.1:443
            env: staging
          - cluster: spoke-production
            url: https://10.200.0.1:443
            env: production
  template:
    metadata:
      name: '{{cluster}}-payment-service'
    spec:
      project: payment-team-project
      source:
        repoURL: 'https://github.com'
        targetRevision: HEAD
        path: apps/payment-service
        helm:
          valueFiles:
            - 'values-shared.yaml'
            - 'values-{{env}}.yaml'
      destination:
        server: '{{url}}'
        namespace: payments
      syncPolicy:
        automated:
          prune: true
          selfHeal: true
```

